WEBVTT

1
00:00:03.400 --> 00:00:07.440
Think of your body as running two completely different supply chains depending on

2
00:00:07.440 --> 00:00:08.440
whether you have just eaten.

3
00:00:08.960 --> 00:00:12.760
In the fed state, blood glucose is abundant, so cells simply burn it.

4
00:00:13.360 --> 00:00:16.140
Glycolysis feeds the Krebs cycle, which makes ATP.

5
00:00:16.140 --> 00:00:21.220
But hours after a meal, glucose runs scarce, and the brain and red blood cells still

6
00:00:21.220 --> 00:00:22.240
demand it constantly.

7
00:00:23.160 --> 00:00:27.800
Now the body switches to gluconeogenesis, manufacturing glucose from non-sugar raw

8
00:00:27.800 --> 00:00:30.560
materials. Three streams feed that factory.

9
00:00:31.320 --> 00:00:36.760
Lactate from muscle and red cells, alanine and glutamine from muscle, and glycerol

10
00:00:36.760 --> 00:00:37.760
from fat breakdown.

11
00:00:38.620 --> 00:00:43.100
Hold onto this fed versus fasted framing because it explains every regulatory

12
00:00:43.100 --> 00:00:44.420
decision we make today.

13
00:00:45.450 --> 00:00:50.950
Most of glycolysis is freely reversible, and gluconeogenesis simply runs those steps

14
00:00:50.950 --> 00:00:56.070
backward. The problem lives in exactly three places where glycolysis releases so

15
00:00:56.070 --> 00:00:59.210
much free energy that the reaction is effectively one-way.

16
00:01:00.050 --> 00:01:05.730
Look at the numbers—hexokinase, phosphofructokinase, and pyruvate kinase—each have

17
00:01:05.730 --> 00:01:10.330
large negative delta ΔG values, so reversing them directly is impossible.

18
00:01:11.370 --> 00:01:16.050
Gluconeogenesis solves this with four dedicated bypass enzymes, shown in orange,

19
00:01:16.810 --> 00:01:22.150
glucose 6 -phosphatase, fructose 1, 6 -bisphosphatase, and the pyruvate carboxylase,

20
00:01:22.150 --> 00:01:24.550
plus PEP carboxykinase pair.

21
00:01:25.430 --> 00:01:30.470
Notice that pyruvate to PEP is split into two reactions, whose combined energetics

22
00:01:30.470 --> 00:01:31.470
make the climb feasible.

23
00:01:32.290 --> 00:01:34.330
Same map, different roads around the cliffs.

24
00:01:35.400 --> 00:01:38.240
Here is a logistics problem the cell must solve.

25
00:01:39.000 --> 00:01:43.880
Pyruvate carboxylase lives inside the mitochondrial matrix, so oxaloacetate is made

26
00:01:43.880 --> 00:01:49.540
there. But the next enzyme, PEP carboxykinase, works in the cytoplasm in this route,

27
00:01:49.880 --> 00:01:52.400
and the membrane has no oxaloacetate transporter.

28
00:01:53.060 --> 00:01:54.320
The workaround is elegant.

29
00:01:55.020 --> 00:01:59.940
Reduce oxaloacetate to malate, which can cross, then reoxidize malate back to

30
00:01:59.940 --> 00:02:01.480
oxaloacetate on the other side.

31
00:02:02.260 --> 00:02:07.840
From pyruvate or alanine, that second oxidation also regenerates cytoplasmic NADH,

32
00:02:08.420 --> 00:02:10.300
which gluconeogenesis needs later.

33
00:02:11.080 --> 00:02:15.820
So one shuttle accomplishes two jobs at once, moving carbon out and delivering

34
00:02:15.820 --> 00:02:20.000
reducing power exactly where the downstream reactions will consume it.

35
00:02:20.933 --> 00:02:25.713
Why does gluconeogenesis need its own enzymes instead of just reversing glycolysis?

36
00:02:26.413 --> 00:02:29.173
Think of it as a bargain the cell strikes with thermodynamics.

37
00:02:29.993 --> 00:02:35.533
Glycolysis releases energy, about 85 kilojoules per mole, so it is downhill and

38
00:02:35.533 --> 00:02:41.193
spontaneous. Gluconeogenesis consumes energy, and that extra cost, the six

39
00:02:41.193 --> 00:02:46.053
nucleotide triphosphate equivalents, is precisely what tips the synthetic direction

40
00:02:46.053 --> 00:02:47.173
to also be favorable.

41
00:02:47.793 --> 00:02:52.573
That means both pathways could run at once in the same cell, a futile cycle that

42
00:02:52.573 --> 00:02:56.013
burns ATP and dumps it as heat with no net product.

43
00:02:57.213 --> 00:03:00.353
Regulation, not the energy cost, is what holds that in check.
